slides.body:
Browser + Node's event loop has this structure (simplified):

```
while (true) {
  task = dequeue(macrotask_queue); // 1 macrotask per turn
  task.run();
  while (microtask_queue.length > 0) {
    microtask_queue.dequeue().run(); // ALL pending microtasks
  }
  render(); // only on browser, only if needed + frame budget allows
}
```

**Macrotasks**: I/O completion, setTimeout / setInterval, UI events (click, keyup), MessageChannel.
**Microtasks**: `Promise.then()` callbacks, `queueMicrotask()`, MutationObserver.

Key property: microtasks run TO COMPLETION before the next macrotask. A promise chain that's still pending when its first `.then` runs will queue another microtask + run synchronously-ish before returning to the loop.

Consequence: a tight loop of promise resolutions can starve macrotasks (UI events) — the browser appears frozen even though it's busy.
